Z(z) = z**2*exp(J) + 2*z*exp(-J) + exp(J)
Z(z)/e^J = z**2 + 2*z*exp(-2*J) + 1   middle coefficient: 2*exp(-2*J)
solve 2 e^{-2J} = a1/sqrt q  =>  J = [log(-sqrt(sqrt(q)/a1)) + log(2)/2, log(sqrt(q)/a1)/2 + log(2)/2]    (requires a1 > 0; for a1 < 0 use the flip z -> -z, i.e. the quadratic twist, a1 -> -a1)
J >= 0  <=>  |a1|/(2 sqrt q) <= 1  <=>  |a1| <= 2 sqrt q  (the Hasse bound, i.e. Weil RH for E).

